Z||000000||loafer87gt||04-09-2001||11:01 PM||||I was just reading on CNN that the E3 surveilance plane was on autopilot when it suposedly swerved at the Chinese fighter. The American crew when interviewed said that the two fighter pilots where doing very agressive manueuvers, and the squadron they belonged to were known for their daredevil antics. If the Chinese would at least let the Americans retrieve the flight recorder (Black box) from the E3, the truth of whether or not the plane veared towards the fighter would be revealed. If this is indeed true that the plane was on autopilot and it was the Chinese pilot who rammed the E3, does that mean that the US gets to demand an apology? Even though I'm up north of the border I'm getting a little peeved about the incident. Heres the latest at CNN<P> <A HREF="http://www.cnn.com/2001/WORLD/asiapcf/east/04/09/air.collision.04/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cnn.com/2001/WORLD/asiapcf/east/04/09/air.collision.04/index.html</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by loafer87gt (edited 04-09-2001).]||||reg||1
