Z||000006||85Josh||04-09-2001||11:45 PM||||Whoa, there, firstfiero, I'm a soldier, and we are not taught to put equipment before life! Those airmen destroyed all the sensitive items inside the plane, and the aircraft commander made  the only choice he could to save his crew. During WWII, many planes landed in German-held territory, and were never charged with treason. That said, I wish that we would quit letting the Chinese play games with our mens lives, and just send in the SEAL's, Rangers, or whoever can do the job! Only problem is, is that China is a nuclear power with more people in their armed services than we have in our entire country. <P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000007||loafer87gt||04-10-2001||12:01 AM||||Yeah, I don't think we'd want to go to war with China, they have 4x as many people as the US. From what I've heard over on the aviation istes I frequent, most of the American planes have some sort of safety "self destruct" measure in case of a situation like this. One guy over at Combatsim said that the computers in the E3 have openings for explosives to be put in case something like this happens. It all comes down to how much time they had between the incident and the landing. The scary thing is that Chinese and Japanese are notorious for reverse engineering stuff. Look at the Mr2 for example! LOL||||reg||1
