Z||000014||Oreif||04-10-2001||11:05 AM||||The Chinese aircraft collided with the E-3 per CNN (E-3 on autopilot). The 2nd Chinese pilot says the E-3 turned in front of them.<BR>Now let's look at it from a non-political view. If I was an E-3 pilot, why would I have the plane on autopilot while I'm being buzzed by 2 Chinese fighters? The E-3 is an "Electronic Survelance" aircraft. So it does not have to "maintain stable flight for pictures" They were in international airspace. (both sides have agreed on this). So I cannot see any reason to be autopilot. The E-3 had to know that the Chinese fighters were there. It's a game that ALL military pilots play (especially fighter pilots). Who can show off the most. The Chinese fighters are a whole lot more manuverable than the E-3. My take on the situation is that the Chinese pilots buzzed the E-3. Either the Chinese fighter got too close and ended up in the prop wash off the turbo props which caused the fighter to lose lift and control and hit the E-3, OR the first fighter buzzed the front of the E-3 and the jet wash caused the E-3 to veer into the second fighter. This means that most likely the fighters were "showing off" and the accident happened. The location of the damage to the E-3 would tell which way it happened. Either way it happened, I would say that the Chinese fighters were too close to the E-3. They were in international airspace heading away from China. The reason China wants an appology is because they want to first, Show the world they are not at fault, and  second, play the political game for their own gains. The U.S. won't because it's obvious that they know which way the accident happened and since the fighters buzzed the E-3 it is automatically China's fault. (in the eyes of the U.S. government)<BR>If this accident would have been between 2 planes from the same country, The fighters would be at fault since they are smaller and more manuverable. They are suppose to allow the slower larger planes the "right of way".<BR>But with the political game both sides are playing this will probably last about 2 more weeks. ||||reg||1
