Z||000021||MotherGoose||04-10-2001||03:21 PM||||First off...KnightRyder we are not back woods people.  Those "terms" for other races and creeds are TOTALLY unacceptable.  We are far to smart to use those terms, after all we drive (or did) drive Fiero's.<P>Next the average age of a fighter pilot isn't in his mid-twenties.  They haven't even gotten out of flight school yet at that age.  And most fighter pilot's do not start off in a fighter.  Only the top people in a class get to pick their plane, the rest start off flying a cargo plane.<P>If they were to "dump" it in the ocean, they would have no time to distroy the equiptment.  As soon as it hit it would start to sink from the damage, and if they weren't in international waters the Chinese would have a better change to get the equiptment intact.<P>The pilot made the right move, it gave them time to distroy everything valuable to the Chinese.<P>Lastly.  A pilot flying a TOP SECRET mission is not a hot dog.  He is number one at what he does.  He hasn't rocked the boat and does things by the book.  If a pilot does pull a stunt, he would be lucky to keep his wings.  No matter how good he is.  To many lives have been lost to stupid pilot's.<P>By the way, it's nice to be back.||||reg||4
