Z||000026||JSocha||04-10-2001||05:11 PM||||I personally think myself that China is pushing for a deliberate conflict (war or not) and this is just one way to start it.<P>After all, isn't it China that has an over population problem to begin with to which they have been trying to resolve with "family" planning which has become a govermental institution program of "one baby" only - if it fails - you're done?  <P>What better way to rapidly reduce a countries popultation levels, blame the death tolls on a war (and of course the country that instigated it wheter true or false) and not be consider by other countries as "barbarians" to their own people.<P>Perfect way to place the blame else where and not in their back yard.<P>Its my opinion now that we, as well as other countries, send our people off to war for the sole purpose when men start to out number women.<P>In my Govermental class in college back in the late 80's, we talked about the wars and the related statistics of "population" density, specifically that of men to women ratios.<P>In every war, didn't matter which country started it, men typically outnumbered women by (what I will now call) a larger then normal margin.<P>After respective wars, women within the countries that were involved in the skirmishes and after all the bloodshed, out numbered men by an almost identical number (I don't have the book anymore otherwise I would quote all of you statistical numbers for battles/wars over the last 150 years and the time period of those wars and how long they lasted).<P>Just a thought to now ponder.  Has anyone else seen the coralation of population as a factor and ratios?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero5a_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||Oreif||04-10-2001||06:56 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MotherGoose:<BR><B><P>Next the average age of a fighter pilot isn't in his mid-twenties.  They haven't even gotten out of flight school yet at that age.  And most fighter pilot's do not start off in a fighter.  Only the top people in a class get to pick their plane, the rest start off flying a cargo plane.<P>A pilot flying a TOP SECRET mission is not a hot dog.  He is number one at what he does.  He hasn't rocked the boat and does things by the book.  If a pilot does pull a stunt, he would be lucky to keep his wings.  No matter how good he is.  To many lives have been lost to stupid pilot's.<P>By the way, it's nice to be back.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The average age of the fighter pilots "worldwide" is mid 20's. True the U.S. pilots are late 20's early 30's. But many countries train there pilots at an earlier<BR>age. The youngest pilots are asian and middle-east. Other countries train their pilots to be fighter pilots first.<P>(Source: Janes book of world aircraft and weapons 1994)<P>Nobody said the U.S. pilot was the "hot dog"<BR>Again you are assuming only the U.S. version. This is an international incident. Not everyone follows the U.S. guidelines in training it's military personnel.<P>Finally, Welcome back!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
